        "claim": "For a veil that steps from `coreAlpha` inside the text column to the listed gutter alpha outside it: the 95th percentile, along each of `columns` evenly spaced columns (a VERTICAL boundary) and each of `rows` evenly spaced rows (a HORIZONTAL one), of the CIE L* difference between the two composites. `spanAtOneJndPx` is 10.5 x the worst of both — the CSS px a smoothstep needs to carry that step with its peak gradient under one JND. Indices are crop fractions: column i spans [i/columns, (i+1)/columns] of the crop WIDTH, row j the same of its HEIGHT, and mapping a CSS coordinate into one of them is `object-fit: cover` arithmetic the consumer owns."
